  "claim_boundary": "For cell-specific strictly increasing response links, shared known midpoint zero is sufficient for the v0.26 offset query to identify each utility threshold independently of link shape. Arbitrary cell-specific midpoint drift is exactly confounded with utility. If midpoint drift is context-only, localized thresholds form a bipartite incidence model: parameters are identified modulo one shift per connected component, cycle rank is the exact liveness dimension for testing the factorization, and the positive Laplacian spectral floor controls Euclidean quotient stability. These are classical Rasch/fixed-effects, incidence, Hodge, pseudoinverse, and threshold-search ingredients specialized into an ASMP-9 access ledger; no novelty is claimed. The result does not establish that real demonstrators share a midpoint, that cardinal offsets are practically available, that a tree validates the context-only model, that finite bisection certifies exact factorization, or that ASMP-9 is resolved.",
